AutoCAD Export - Katapult Engineering

[Katapult Logo]

# AutoCAD Export

Modified on: Tue, 7 Jun, 2022 at 11:09 AM

Katapult Pro has the ability to export your data to AutoCAD. To use this feature, please navigate to your Export page.

**Step 1: Choose a Template**

In order to export to AutoCAD, you must first set up an **AutoCAD Template**. You select the template here.

The AutoCAD export feature converts your Katapult data into AutoCAD format, but the output **requires significant manual cleanup and formatting** to meet permit-ready or construction-ready standards. Templates can be customized, but the result is often not directly usable without additional drafting work.

**Step 2: Export Your Data**

After choosing your template, select the nodes, connections, or entire job that you want to export. Click the **Export** button to begin.

**Step 3: Review the Output**

The resulting DWG file will contain your GIS data as AutoCAD entities. **Note:** Annotation placement, layer standards, title blocks, and drawing conventions may require manual adjustment per client or permit authority requirements.

